Changes made in this fork:

  * package, Cordis row, panel, storage identity and route namespace renamed to
    dsh-deep-seek; saved state moved to its own directory, so no credential
    file written by another plugin is read or reused;
  * sidebar glyph replaced with a plain chat-bubble outline on the shell's 16 px
    grid, drawn with the same 1.3 px currentColor line as the official rows;
  * the panel is the page: no header, toolbar or status row is drawn around the
    guest, and the page is always laid out at 90 %;
  * that zoom is applied with Chromium's own `setZoomFactor`, so page layout
    scales instead of being CSS-transformed;
  * request-race guards: a lease acquired after teardown is released, and the
    guest no longer posts a "releasing" save while being disposed;
  * plugin stylesheet is removed and the guest released when the plugin unloads.

Upstream itself states it was inspired by jaychang1989/dsh-webchat and
xmuwenxiang/dsh-web-chat (both Apache-2.0); see the upstream NOTICE for that
attribution, which this fork keeps in effect.

The glyph is drawn for this fork; no third-party icon file is reproduced.
